# AGENT.md — src/

Application root for the Onion Architecture on Express.

## What lives here

- `main.ts` — starts the server{{#if hasOrm}} and initializes the ORM connection{{/if}}.
- `app.ts` — composition root. Builds the Express app, wires all dependencies
  manually, registers middleware and routes.
- `config/` — environment loading, swagger setup.
- `middlewares/` — error handler, validation middlewares.
- `errors/` — AppError base class and subclasses (NotFoundError, ValidationError).
- `shared/` — cross-cutting infrastructure (database, cache{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if useHealthCheck}}, health{{/if}}).

## Onion Architecture layers

```
src/
├── domain/          ← Innermost: entities, repository interfaces (ports)
├── application/     ← Use cases, DTOs, service implementations
├── infrastructure/  ← Persistence adapters (TypeORM, Prisma, Mongoose, in-memory)
└── presentation/    ← Outermost: Express controllers and route definitions
```

## Rules

- Do not put business logic in `main.ts` or `app.ts`.
- When you add a new module, register its routes in `app.ts` with
  `app.use('/path', moduleRoutes(controller))`.
- All middleware is applied in `app.ts` in order: global → routes → error handler.
{{#if useAuth}}
- Auth middleware (`authenticate`) is available in `shared/auth/auth.middleware.ts`.
  Attach it to protected route handlers via `router.get('/', authenticate, controller.handler)`.
{{/if}}
